      "title": "Surrogate credentials, nothing paired yet — 390 × 844",
      "caption": "An unlocked vault on a dedicated origin opens Settings › Capabilities with both plugin capabilities on. Before, the tile can only say no daemon is paired: the page had no way to reach the plugin routes. After, the same tile carries the pairing field and one icon key.",
      "before": "mark only; no field, no way to pair",
      "after": "Pairing code field + Pair with the daemon key"
    },
    {
      "shot": "390-installed-off",
      "width": 390,
      "title": "Paired: the surrogate proxy installed, off — 390 × 844",
      "caption": "The code opensesame plugins pair printed is pasted and traded once for this page's own key; the daemon answers GET /v1/plugins. Before, the paste had nowhere to go and the tile is unchanged.",
      "before": "No daemon paired",
      "after": "Installed, off; host and version; switch; forget key"
    },
    {
      "shot": "390-on",
      "width": 390,
      "title": "Switched on from Settings — 390 × 844",
      "caption": "The switch sends PUT /v1/plugins/surrogate-proxy with the paired key; the daemon re-verifies the install pin and answers on. The tripwires the plugin recorded are listed by event, time and subject — never a surrogate.",
      "before": "No daemon paired",
      "after": "On, with two tripwires"
    },
    {
      "shot": "390-forced-off",
      "width": 390,
      "title": "Browser autofill forced off on the daemon — 390 × 844",
      "caption": "The daemon's environment says OPENSESAME_PLUGIN_BROWSER_AUTOFILL=off, so the file's on does not count: the tile wears the warning mark and its switch is locked. Nothing on this page can turn on what the operator turned off.",
      "before": "No daemon paired",
      "after": "Forced off on the daemon; switch disabled"
    },
